LeCun指出，AI研究者并不具备讨论技术革命对就业影响的资格，应该听取真正研究这一问题的劳动经济学家的意见。他强调，虽然短期内可能会有岗位被取代，但长期来看，工作任务会被重构，新的岗位也会随之产生。他反对AI圈内的末日营销，认为这种恐慌会误导公众和政策，呼吁大家关注如何利用AI提升自身价值。

@ylecun: "Dario is wrong. He knows absolutely nothing about the effects of technological revolutions on the labor market. Don't listen to him, Sam, Yoshua, Geoff, or me on this topic. Listen to economists who have spent their career studying this, like @Ph_Aghion, @erikbryn, @DAcemogluMIT, @amcafee, @davidautor."

Russia eased vaccination standards when diphtheria seemed beaten, resulting in 157,000 infections and 5,000 deaths. Japan dropped mandates after a trust collapse, leading to a resurgence of rubella and babies being born blind and deaf. Nigeria boycotted polio shots, causing paralysis in 2,500 children and the virus spreading to 20 countries.

Kennedy has now dropped six vaccines from routine schedules and pulled $1.6 billion from global immunization efforts, with measles already present in 46 states. The linked article discusses how vaccine skepticism, fueled by government actions, risks a return of preventable diseases.

@propublica: "Vaccines were once so uncontroversial that McDonald’s restaurants put the childhood immunization schedule on their tray liners. Now, as the U.S. government sows doubt, preventable diseases could come roaring back."

More people will die from suppressing AI than from the imaginary AI apocalypse. They will die from restricting safe self-driving cars, which are 90% better drivers than humans, contributing to 1.5 million deaths and 50 million injuries annually. They will also die from vaccines and cures that never get created, and from helpful inventions that geniuses in data centers could have developed.

Preventable diseases will claim lives because people won't be able to consult chatbots for better information before visiting doctors due to restrictive legislation. The economy will suffer from stifled robot-driven factories due to exaggerated fears of job loss, preventing the creation of affordable goods. Cheaper solar panels and batteries that could be produced by these automated factories will also be delayed, impacting climate change and access to energy in underserved areas. Additionally, super smart tele-AI doctors will never reach remote areas, and the radicalization of the anti-AI movement could lead to violence.

